---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout class="homepage">
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>👋 Welcome to ShapeThing</h1>
      <p class="tagline"><strong>Your data has stories to tell. We help you bring them together.</strong></p>
      <p>
        ShapeThing is a simple, friendly tool that helps you organize, link, and explore your data — no tech background
        required.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section what-is">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>🧩 What’s ShapeThing All About?</h2>
      <p>Think of ShapeThing as a smart workspace where you can:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Create custom data forms that fit your world</li>
        <li>Link related things together (people, places, events — you name it!)</li>
        <li>Keep everything neat, structured, and searchable</li>
        <li>Export and share your data in open-friendly formats</li>
      </ul>
      <p>No complicated setups, no coding. Just you and your data — organized your way.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section features">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>🌟 Why People Love ShapeThing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Easy to Use</strong> – Everything happens in your browser. No installs, no fuss.</li>
        <li><strong>Made for Humans</strong> – Use plain language and clear forms instead of cryptic codes.</li>
        <li><strong>Connect the Dots</strong> – See how your data fits together with visual tools.</li>
        <li><strong>Works With the Web</strong> – Your data stays portable, open, and future-ready.</li>
        <li><strong>Built for Collaboration</strong> – Invite others, share your models, and work together.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section audience">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>👥 Who's It For?</h2>
      <p>ShapeThing is for anyone who wants to make sense of complex information, like:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Researchers & Students</li>
        <li>Archivists & Librarians</li>
        <li>Writers & Curators</li>
        <li>Data tinkerers & toolmakers</li>
        <li>Anyone working on digital projects with people, places, or ideas</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section capabilities">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>🛠️ What Can You Do?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Design custom forms for your data</li>
        <li>Link entries to each other and to the wider web</li>
        <li>Search, browse, and explore relationships</li>
        <li>Export your data to use elsewhere</li>
        <li>Validate your data and keep it tidy</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .homepage .site-main {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2em;
  }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .homepage .site-main {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      grid-template-rows: repeat(5, auto);
      grid-template-areas: 'header header' 'left right';
    }
  }

  .homepage .hero {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: 2em;

    h1 {
      color: var(--purple);
    }
  }
  .homepage .hero:after {
    display: block;
    position: absolute;
    background-color: var(--blue-light);
    width: 100vw;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    opacity: 0.1;
    height: 100%;
    content: '';
    z-index: -1;
    top: 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .homepage .hero {
      grid-area: header;
    }
  }
</style>
